From 99e886bbc76c3684523478bb47169281ab008f6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Derek J. Clark" <derekjohn.clark@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 20:22:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] feat: add generic capability translation to the evdev
 translator

Unify the V1 and V2 capability-map translation paths into one state
machine in the evdev layer. The composite device will stop translating
evdev events in a later commit; for now source drivers receive the
source-level map only, so there is no double translation.

- Add src/input/event/evdev/maps.rs which adds MappingKind and
  MappedTranslation types.
- Rewrite src/input/event/evdev/translator.rs as the unified
  EventTranslator.
- Normalize composite and source level V1/V1 configs into a single
  mapping list that lives on the source device.
- Chords now have a 20 ms deferral grace window if they are a subset of
  another chord.
- Add proper resolution-based IMU scaling.
- Debounce release holds via try_emit.
- Move the EventCapability trait from the source layer to the event
  layer (src/input/event/mod.rs) and re-export it from source.
- Load the source-level map as V1 or V2 in the evdev factory.
- Warn on unknown map ids.
- Wire the translator into the gamepad, keyboard, and touchscreen
  evdev drivers.
- get_capabilities() reports post-translation capabilities from the source.
- Drop delayed chord handling. It was broken and unused, now replaced with
  automatic deferral detection.

Behavior notes: source-level V1 maps now apply for the first time;
on-demand filters on mapped sources match post-translation
capabilities; the 16ms minimum release window now applies to all
translated outputs.
