From 16b23231231179adccecb459b18691750d8d718e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Derek J. Clark" <derekjohn.clark@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 10:39:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] feat: Push combined capability map into sources, remove
 composite translation

The composite device no longer translates events. The combined map
is now pushed into the evdev source drivers, which build their
EventTranslator directly.

- EventDevice::new() takes the composite-level map, combines it with the
  source-level map via maps::from_maps, and passes the result to the
  gamepad, keyboard, and touchscreen drivers
- Delete CompositeDevice::translate_capability(), load_capability_map(),
  the event-loop translation check, and the translatable_capabilities,
  translatable_active_inputs, and emitted_mappings state. Mapped evdev
  sources now report post-translation capabilities themselves.
- DBus send_event floor: replace translated_recent_events with
  recent_events: HashMap<Capability, Instant> gated by
  translator::try_emit; a held release is re-injected via WriteEvent at
  press_time + 16 ms
- Delete the CompositeCommand::HandleEvent and RemoveRecentEvent variants
  and their dead client wrappers

Behavioral notes: Non-evdev sources with composite-level maps no longer
translate; oxp5 QuickAccess-from-HID and flydigi-vader-4-pro
paddle-to-touchpad V1 maps are inert until a hidraw translation layer
exists.
