From fcc0774f46c661dfdfaae06ebdf258af8ad0c02a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Derek J. Clark" <derekjohn.clark@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 06:47:33 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] feat: account for every kernel input event code

Every KEY_*, BTN_*, ABS_*, and REL_* code in the kernel's
input-event-codes.h now maps to a Capability and back. Previously,
unmapped codes were mapped to NotImplemented and were dropped. Now all
valid kernel events will be able to pass through or be mapped, even if
they don't have an analogous usage in InputPumber defined targets.

- Add raw catch-all variants per category: Keyboard::Raw, Mouse::Raw,
  MouseButton::Raw, GamepadButton::Raw, GamepadAxis::Raw, plus explicit
  variants for the practical codes (Button0..9, Trigger, TriggerHappy,
  Back, Forward, Throttle, Rudder, Wheel, Gas, Brake).
- Replace the NotImplemented arms in EvdevEvent::to_capability with the
  explicit variants; the wildcards become range-classified catch-alls so
  codes beyond the header defines space round-trip too.
- Extend the reverse event code tables symmetrically.
- BTN_Z now maps to GamepadButton::Raw(0x135) instead of QuickAccess,
  which has no evdev output codes and could not round-trip.
- Capability maps can reference raw codes: EventCode accepts a numeric
  value alongside named defines (event_code: 0x12c), and map configs
  accept the catch-all capability strings (e.g. button: Raw(0x130)).
  Regenerate the capability map v2 JSON schema.
- Fix the KeyKpdot FromStr typo and the Mouse::Raw FromStr arm so all
  capability strings round-trip.

Assisted-by: LLM
